{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\nThe force-close hint advertises a no-force path for administrative dispositions:\n> Hint: if this close is administrative (duplicate / obsolete / superseded / wontfix rather than completed work), --class <value> closes it through the attested disposition path — obsolete/wontfix with --reason=<text> ... no --force needed.\n\nBut in practice on task ticket 192c-d606-b72e-470f (brokendown-graceless-pelican, invalid premise), `rebar transition <id> open closed --class obsolete --reason=...` fails with `plan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation`. A signed BLOCK plan-review still cannot satisfy the gate, so invalid-premise task tickets are structurally unclosable without operator force. Bug-type administrative closes have been observed to close gate-free through the same --class path.\n\n## Prior-art decision to revise\nBug 69b9 deliberately exempted only link-backed administrative classes (`duplicate`, `superseded`) from the plan-review close gate because those have verifiable replacement-link evidence. Since then, `close_disposition.verdict()` gained deterministic reason-backed disposition attestations for `obsolete` and `wontfix`: the close reason is recorded as `close_reason` and signed into the completion-verifier/disposition manifest. This ticket does not add a plain prose-only bypass; it extends the plan-review close gate to recognize the same deterministic disposition attestation that the completion close path already mints, and it must validate class/reason/replacement requirements before granting the exemption.\n\n## Hypothesis\nThe plan-review close gate runs before the completion precheck's close-class validation and its exemption predicate only checks `_LINK_BACKED_DISPOSITION_CLASSES`. Therefore reason-backed administrative dispositions reach the plan-review gate as ordinary completed-work closes and fail on missing PASS plan-review. The fix is to (1) run the shared `txn.close_class_refusal()` validation before the plan-review close recheck, (2) thread `close_reason` into `_plan_review_close_recheck()` / `gates.close_plan_review_gate_check()`, and (3) have the gate reuse `close_disposition.verdict()` for all administrative classes so obsolete/wontfix are exempt only when a signable reason-backed disposition exists.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py -q` includes a RED regression where an open task with plan-review close gate enabled closes as `--class obsolete --reason=...` without `--force`; before the fix it raises the plan-review attestation error, after the fix it succeeds and records `close_class=obsolete` plus the reason-backed disposition attestation.\n- [ ] Completed-work closes without `--class` still require the existing certified plan-review/completion-verifier path; the regression suite proves that normal closes are not weakened.\n- [ ] Administrative disposition closes (`obsolete`, `wontfix`, `duplicate`, `superseded`) bypass the plan-review close gate for non-bug and bug tickets only after `txn.close_class_refusal()` / `close_disposition.verdict()` accepts the class/reason/replacement evidence.\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` and the CLI hint agree that administrative/attested-disposition closes do not need force and do not require a PASSING plan-review attestation.\n\n## Testing\n- RED/GREEN: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py -q`\n- Focused full close-path coverage: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py tests/unit/test_close_gate_disposition_69b9.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_transition_reason_honest_3803.py -q`\n- Full verification before push: `env -u GIT_CONFIG_COUNT -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_2 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_2 PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788861444104074001,"uuid":"5ef092f0-8b12-4202-8c4e-a490082ccf4e"}